 "description": "QUESTION_DRIVER_RUNG3_PREREG.md / _RESULTS.md: a ProblemShape codebook recognizing the STRUCTURAL SHAPE of an already-minted solve_* Goal (domains/solver_dispatch.py) from its own real attrs/edges (never from its kind string), via the UNCHANGED ShapeDecode Term pointed at codebook_type='ProblemShape' (load_parts is grain-agnostic -- confirmed at runners/dsl/src/shape_decode.rs, re-confirmed here). ProblemShape is a NEW node type (not a ShapeSignature{kind:...}), mirroring the DirectionalCorrespondence precedent (analogical_thinking.py:672-687): ShapeDecode's live decode pool does not partition on kind, so a kind-tagged ShapeSignature would silently compete for inference_generation.resolve_implication_gap's real decode slot. Two shapes (deduction_shape, can_shape) are SEEDED, grounded in >=5 real recurring dispatch instances each (QUESTION_DRIVER_RUNG3_PREREG.md Sec1.1); a third (decompose_shape) is DELIBERATELY left unseeded to mint live from real recurrence (2 real solve_decompose instances -- the same support=2 floor META_SHAPE_FIRST_CLASS_RESULTS.md Sec4.1 already established as 'the smallest cardinality at which recurs is defined'). Rung 1 uses literal ShapeDecode (Count(residual)==0), NOT Covers -- every signature here is fully concrete, no WILD, unlike meta-shape's anti-unified lgg codebook (Sec4.1 of the prereg explains why Covers is unneeded here). Mint (rung 4) uses ONLY existing generic Terms (Eq/Exists/Argmin/Count/Plus -- the SAME canonical-minter idiom seeds/gap_awareness.json::retire_duplicate_gap already uses), not a bespoke Rust Term: every real solve_decompose observation produces the IDENTICAL literal signature, so anti-unifying two of them is a no-op and minting directly from the observation's own signature is correct. Rungs 2/3 (TransformDecode/DimInfer) are NOT wired -- a graceful, deliberate no-op (every axis here is a categorical presence/value string, never an integer coordinate; QUESTION_DRIVER_RUNG3_PREREG.md Sec4.1), mirroring META_SHAPE_FIRST_CLASS_RESULTS.md Sec3's own rung-3 no-op. The hold-open multi-candidate layer and pre-mint auto-dispatch are explicitly OUT of scope this rung (QUESTION_DRIVER_RUNG3_PREREG.md Sec5) -- no real case of genuine candidate competition, and no real raw-problem corpus, exists yet to ground either.",
